WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
(lively music)
- Carhartt,

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.240
the company has been a
part of streetwear culture,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.370
as long as streetwear has been around.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.670
Drake, Rihanna, and Obama are
only a few of the big names

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.230
who have donned the brand.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.370
- It's worn by folks

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.530
that might be wearing
Carhartt to tech jobs,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.700
or might be wearing Carhartt

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.860
as they trade crypto on the daily.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.530
- [Narrator] But Carhartt didn't
chase after this consumer.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.910
And its popularity in fashion

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.550
has little to do with
the company's strategy.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.380
In fact, the workwear brand strategy

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.710
has been rather consistent
across 134 years,

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.083
even while its competition changed course.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.428
This is the economics of Carhartt.

00:00:34.428 --> 00:00:35.820
(lively music)
When Carhartt

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.860
was founded in 1889,
(camera shutter clicks)

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.950
the American workforce looked
pretty different than today's.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.000
At the turn of the century,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.370
an estimated 38% worked on farms,

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:48.210
and 31% worked in mining,
manufacturing, and construction.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.350
When a traveling salesman
(camera shutter clicks)

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.630
named, Hamilton Carhartt
asked railroad workers

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.700
how their uniforms could be improved,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.930
he used his findings to create

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.850
the first Carhartt product,
(camera shutter clicks)

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.110
a pair of overalls.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.500
- These are some of our
early styles of overalls

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.570
from the earliest years of the company.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.880
- [Narrator] Overtime, Carhartt expanded.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.680
- We start making work pants,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.720
which at the time were
called waist overalls.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.510
We started introducing jackets and coats.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:13.590
- [Narrator] The overalls chore coat

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.610
and the double front pant,

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.710
laid the groundwork for Carhartt's brand,

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.050
and they've remained relatively unchanged.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.120
- We always have those core products.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.170
We always have that denim.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.430
We always have that duck.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.660
It's always gonna be something

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.370
that you're gonna be able to get from us.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.730
Having that foundation
is what allows us to do

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.374
some of the experimentation we do.

00:01:31.374 --> 00:01:32.700
(lively music)
- As the workforce evolved

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.340
and the number of railroad
workers and farmers dwindled,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.440
experimentation was key.
(camera shutter clicks)

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.350
And Carhartt's consumers
gave the brand an idea.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.240
Today, there is no article of clothing

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.940
that better represents Carhartt
than what's known internally

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.630
as the A18 Watch Hat, aka the beanie.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.370
Google searches for
Carhartt and its beanie

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.500
have increased over recent years.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.600
At 1999, the beanies are priced

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.790
as an entry point for
first-time customers,

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.030
and are a top-selling item
for the brand each year.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.110
- Carhartt's popularity right now

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.250
is best described as this
thirst for authenticity.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.260
This thirst for genuine clothing.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.490
The way fashion works right now,

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:12.240
it's not necessarily that
one trend is super dominant.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.980
Carhartt is finding purchase

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.800
with a lot of different
waves of trend right now.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.000
- [Narrator] And it's not the first time

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.006
the family owned company
exploded into the mainstream.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:23.238
♪ Jump around ♪

00:02:23.238 --> 00:02:24.458
♪ Jump around ♪

00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:25.500
- [Narrator] In the '80s and '90s,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.660
Dickies and Carhartt were
picked up by skateboarders

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.460
and famous rappers as streetwear.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.840
- That had a trickle down effect.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.070
Once rappers were wearing it,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.690
then other people wanted it as well.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.460
- [Narrator] Dickies
leaned into the attention.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.510
On its Instagram page,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.700
you'll find photos of
farmers and woodworkers,

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.310
but you'll also see a
lot of skateboarders.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.560
Whereas Carhartt almost exclusively shows

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.020
people working in its clothes.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.090
Dickies also expanded its product lines,

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.070
adding more options for skateboarders.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.940
Today, it has a total of
159 men's pants and shorts,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.260
and its original 874 work
pants come in 21 colors.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.670
Carhartt, on the other hand,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.510
sells 67 items under the men's
work pants in short section.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.040
This includes items like jeans

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.930
and a single pair of sweatpants.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:10.110
At most, it makes a pair
of pants in eight colors,

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.810
but many have between two to four options.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.370
While Carhartt's websites and stores

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.720
are important for the company,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.150
they're not yet the company's
biggest source of revenue.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.250
Instead, the brand still relies heavily

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.650
on wholesale distribution
to other retailers,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.630
like Tractor Supply,
Dick's Sporting Goods,

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.160
and Bass Pro Shops.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.820
But recently, Carhartt explored
a new way to reach workers.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.520
- So in 2018, we started
Carhartt company gear,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.080
because there was a consumer need

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.540
to provide uniform that can be embellished

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.880
with different company's logos and names.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.810
- [Narrator] Not long after,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.640
it partnered with United Airlines

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.370
providing uniforms to 28,000 workers.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.890
And in 2023, Carhartt
and "The Weather Channel"

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.690
announced a partnership.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.890
While Carhartt has presented

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.080
an unwavering devotion to workwear,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.640
there is a caveat.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.610
Back in the late 1980s,
when streetwear took off,

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.550
a European retailer made
the company a proposal.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.990
He'd take Carhartt's merchandise

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.420
and tweak it for a European audience.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.260
Carhartt agreed.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.920
And in 1989, all-American
concept was born.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.100
Soon after it was renamed to
Carhartt Work In Progress.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.230
As a licensee, Carhartt Work in Progress

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.210
caters to anyone interested in streetwear

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.610
and other apparel inspired by workwear.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.760
And in 2011, it expanded to the US.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.650
Importantly, Carhartt Work in Progress

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.390
still reports to Carhartt.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.710
They make decisions together,

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.190
and Work in Progress' revenue
is a portion of Carhartt's.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.320
- It's been really wonderful
to have the licensee

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.850
with Carhartt Work in Progress,

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.490
and it does allow them to
address a different consumer,

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.710
but it's still inspired by workwear.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.570
So that allows Carhartt, for us,

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.570
to really focus in on
building the most durable

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.240
and versatile workwear for the job sites.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.270
- Versatility is really
something that our consumer

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.970
has seemed to have created
kind of on their own.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.460
We start off as this
workwear company, right?

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.270
And we, all of a sudden, you
know, see our stuff being used

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.210
in the outdoors, camping, hunting,

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.430
you know, all those other kinds of of uses

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.354
for like a rugged, heavy-duty product.

00:05:04.354 --> 00:05:05.340
(camera shutter clicks)
- Seeing this

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.040
inspired Carhartt to
create a new product line

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.170
called Super Dux in the 1930s
(camera shutter clicks)

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.360
for all these other outdoor uses.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.460
But this line didn't take off back then.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.890
People already had outdoor
jackets from Carhartt,

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.120
their work jackets.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.740
They didn't need another one.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.930
Still, Carhartt learned something key.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.700
It's workwear clothing was being used

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.713
for far more than just work.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.990
Over the course of a few decades,

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.460
this revelation changed workwear

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.548
and the original companies that made it.

00:05:31.548 --> 00:05:34.950
In the 1970s, Carhartt expanded
beyond outdoor apparel,

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.390
starting with a sweatshirt

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.940
- We can go out and make a
t-shirt, or make a beanie,

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:42.420
or maybe play around with some
sort of contemporary styles.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:43.770
- [Narrator] This mindset
defined the company

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.300
over the century and helped to grow

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.890
even while many Americans pivoted

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.350
from working outdoors to offices.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.290
- There were many workwear
manufacturers in America

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.160
at a certain time.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.920
And a lot of them, for
a multitude of reasons,

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.240
have fallen away.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.320
They don't exist anymore.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.340
They've gone bankrupt.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.610
They've been subsumed
by a different company,

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.280
and those clothes just
aren't existent anymore.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.140
- [Narrator] Work and the way
people think about clothing

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.320
has changed significantly in 134 years.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.030
But Carhartt hasn't.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.120
- Just 'cause someone wears
something for a utilitarian job

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.200
doesn't mean they're not thinking

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.570
about how that product
looks on their body.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.850
This kind of fashion consumer
and this function consumer,

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.670
I think they cross over
in a lot of places.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.700
And, you know, you might
have the Carhartt jacket

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.930
'cause it looks really cool,

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.330
but then on a 30-degree day, you might be

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.003
really happy you have it.
(gentle music)

